  "faqs": [
    {
      "question": "Do AI trainers get paid?",
      "answer": "Yes, verified platforms pay AI trainers hourly or per task for completed, approved work. Payments are distributed through processors like PayPal, Stripe, Wise, Airtm, or direct ACH transfer, though task availability varies."
    },
    {
      "question": "Is AI training a legitimate job?",
      "answer": "Yes, AI training is legitimate freelance contract work for major technology labs. You work as an independent 1099 contractor rather than a W-2 employee, meaning you receive no employment benefits, paid leave, or guaranteed weekly hours."
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the easiest AI job to get?",
      "answer": "Platforms like Prolific and Mindrift offer the lowest barrier to entry, requiring general English fluency and basic reading comprehension rather than advanced academic credentials. Handshake AI and Mercor require graduate degrees, published work, or technical coding expertise."
    },
    {
      "question": "Can I get an AI job with no experience?",
      "answer": "Yes, general annotation and prompt-evaluation projects on platforms like Mindrift or Prolific accept beginners who pass an initial reading and writing screening test. Technical projects in software engineering, law, and medicine require verified professional credentials or degrees."
    },
    {
      "question": "How much do AI trainers make?",
      "answer": "Pay ranges from $15 to $30 per hour for entry-level tasks on Mindrift to over $85 per hour on Mercor according to TechCrunch. Highly specialized coding or STEM projects on DataAnnotation advertise rates starting at $40 to $150 or more per hour."
    },
    {
      "question": "Do AI training jobs send a 1099?",
      "answer": "Yes, US contractors earning reportable freelance income receive a tax form from the platform or its payment processor. For example, Mercor provides a Form 1099-NEC through Stripe for contractors who submit a Form W-9 and earn more than $600 during the tax year."
